<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb corn imports down 10.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb corn imports down 10.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's corn imports in February totalled 1,175,293 tonnes, down 10.6 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>			  Feb 97	  Jan 97	  Feb 96</p>
<p> Total		1,175,293     1,333,733     1,314,318</p>
<p> Feed corn total    781,178	 870,016	 853,707</p>
<p> Others		 394,115	 463,717	 460,611</p>
<p>Top suppliers of feed corn (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		   781,178	 859,934	 853,707</p>
<p>Total feed corn imports during the first two months of calendar 1997 reached 1,651,194 tonnes against 1,609,133 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk (+81-3 3432-7391)</p>
</text>
